    "created_at": "2022-02-17T11:53:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-17T11:53:55Z",
    "body": "\"The element's [checkedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fe-checked) state is set to true (for whatever reason).\" includes programmatic modifications. Though this is action at a distance, so not ideal.\r\n\r\nI believe the dirty checkedness difference is intentional, but if browsers don't agree then maybe it can be changed.\r\n\r\nThe dirty checkedness is checked (no pun intended) when setting or removing the `checked` content attribute:\r\n\r\n> When the [checked](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-checked) content attribute is added, if the control does not have [dirty checkedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-input-checked-dirty), the user agent must set the [checkedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fe-checked) of the element to true; when the [checked](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-checked) content attribute is removed, if the control does not have [dirty checkedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-input-checked-dirty), the user agent must set the [checkedness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fe-checked) of the element to false.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-input-checked\r\n\r\nDemo:\r\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=10054\r\n",
